sections.body:
Kredit provides tools that allow an existing seller and customer to:

• record the goods, price, payment day, extra time and any payment plan;
• show the same terms to the customer before the customer says yes;
• keep evidence of acceptance, goods release and customer receipt;
• record payments made to the seller or through an approved provider;
• show the amount still unpaid;
• send account and payment reminders;
• report and review a problem; and
• request an authorised bank debit for an eligible unpaid amount after the agreed time.

Kredit is not the seller and does not supply the goods. Kredit does not choose the customer, decide the quality of goods or promise that a customer will pay. The supplier funds the credit sale. The seller supplies its own goods and allows payment later.

Kredit is not a bank, wallet, credit bureau, insurance company, marketplace or debt buyer. Any regulated identity, banking or payment function must be performed through an appropriately approved provider. A provider's own terms may also apply to that function.

You must use Kredit honestly, follow applicable law and cooperate with a reasonable check or correction. You must not:

• create a false person, business, sale, delivery, payment, receipt or dispute;
• use another person's contact, bank or identity information without authority;
• sell illegal, unsafe, stolen or prohibited goods through a Kredit record;
• split, repeat or manipulate a sale to avoid a limit or review;
• attempt to collect money already paid, reversed, adjusted or genuinely disputed;
• harass, threaten, shame or mislead a seller or customer;
• probe, copy, damage or interfere with Kredit or another user's account;
• upload malware or a document you have no right to use; or
• use Kredit to hide fraud, money laundering or another unlawful activity.

Kredit may limit a document type, transaction size, customer group, business industry, provider, retry or other service feature. A displayed limit does not mean Kredit has approved a customer's creditworthiness or guaranteed a transaction.

Subject to the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and any lawful exception, you may:

• ask whether Kredit uses your personal information;
• ask to see it and receive a copy;
• ask us to correct information that is wrong or incomplete;
• ask us to remove information when there is no lawful reason to keep it;
• ask us to limit a use while a concern is checked;
• object to a use based on legitimate interests or direct marketing;
• withdraw consent where consent is the reason for the use;
• ask for portable information in a usable format where applicable;
• ask for an explanation of a significant automated decision and request human review; and
• complain to Kredit or the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.

Open Your information (https://kredit.ng/app/settings/privacy) after signing in to send a request and follow its progress. We will verify the requester before releasing or changing private information. We may keep a limited record that a request was completed. If we cannot do everything requested, we will explain the lawful reason.
